```ts
function groupBy<T, K extends keyof T>(items: readonly T[], key: K): Map<T[K], T[]> {
  const out = new Map<T[K], T[]>();
  for (const item of items) {
    const k = item[key];
    const list = out.get(k);
    if (list) list.push(item); else out.set(k, [item]);
  }
  return out;
}
```
`K extends keyof T` ties the key to the item type; `T[K]` is an indexed access type. Using `readonly T[]` accepts both mutable and readonly arrays. A Map avoids prototype keys and allows non-string keys.

